1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,691
DarkCall is a sealed-bid auction on Zcash where no bid is ever opened, yet the price is proven and paid out in one shielded transaction.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,545
Normally, checking the price means someone reads the bids:

3
00:00:12,545 --> 00:00:15,602
everyone after the close, or whoever makes the proof.

4
00:00:15,602 --> 00:00:18,140
And a proven price doesn't prove the payout.

5
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:20,987
Let's run one, live.

6
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:22,814
A seller lists three units.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:31,625
Each bidder's client splits its bid into three secret shares, one per operator, and proves in zero knowledge that they match its commitment.

8
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:35,487
Operators check the proof and sign a receipt, but none can read a bid.

9
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:42,469
At the deadline, the operators certify the book.

10
00:00:42,469 --> 00:00:49,522
All three clear it on the shares with REP3, and coNoir turns that into one proof of the price, in about eight seconds.

11
00:00:49,522 --> 00:00:52,092
Nobody rebuilds a bid, not even the prover.

12
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,217
Twenty-one per unit, three sold.

13
00:00:55,217 --> 00:00:57,612
Each bidder opens only its own result.

14
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,279
That run had no deposits.

15
00:01:00,279 --> 00:01:04,259
On October 19th the same four bids ran on public Zcash testnet:

16
00:01:04,259 --> 00:01:12,725
shielded deposits into a two-of-three FROST escrow, six Halo2 proofs binding every payout to the result, and one shielded transaction.

17
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:15,287
Here is that settlement.

18
00:01:15,287 --> 00:01:17,468
Bidder one decrypts its own receipt:

19
00:01:17,468 --> 00:01:18,923
one unit, at twenty-one.

20
00:01:18,923 --> 00:01:21,589
Everyone else sees one shielded transaction.

21
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:23,620
Bidder four:

22
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,231
no unit, full refund.

23
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,709
Anyone can re-verify it with no secrets:

24
00:01:29,709 --> 00:01:34,538
the price proof, six payout proofs, the signed book and the Zcash signatures.

25
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,326
Now try to cheat.

26
00:01:38,326 --> 00:01:39,916
Change one accepted bid:

27
00:01:39,916 --> 00:01:41,705
the signed book refuses it.

28
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,147
Claim a higher price:

29
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,879
the price proof refuses it.

30
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,170
Private inputs, public checks.

31
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:58,591
Every run is recorded in the repository, and make verify checks it on your own machine.
